@startuml fig03_deployment
!include theme.iuml
title Figure 3 — Deployment View: Heterogeneous Pool on a Trusted LAN

skinparam nodesep 26
skinparam ranksep 55

node "harness-host" #FFFCF5 {
  artifact "config.yaml + seed" as CFG
  artifact "trace.jsonl" as TR
  artifact "run_manifest.json" as RM
  component "replay.py\nopen-loop · no runtime RNG" as REP
  component "Thin Client" as CLI
}

node "sched-host" {
  component "Scheduler\nPython + asyncio · control plane only" as SCHED
}

cloud "Trusted LAN\nno authentication boundary" as LAN

node "node-A\ndiscrete GPU · class G1" as NA {
  component "Worker Wrapper" as WA
  component "llama.cpp · GGUF 7-8B\n-ngl 99" as EA <<reused>>
}
node "node-B\nolder GPU · class G2" as NB {
  component "Worker Wrapper" as WB
  component "llama.cpp · GGUF 7-8B\n-ngl 40" as EB <<reused>>
}
node "node-C\nlaptop GPU · class G3" as NC {
  component "Worker Wrapper" as WC
  component "llama.cpp · GGUF 7-8B\n-ngl 20" as EC <<reused>>
}
node "node-D\nCPU only · class C1" as ND {
  component "Worker Wrapper" as WD
  component "llama.cpp · GGUF 7-8B\n-ngl 0 · threads only" as ED <<reused>>
}

rectangle "vLLM · AWQ 7-8B on node-A\none operating point, identical replayed trace" as VGAP <<measured condition, not a pool member>> #F3F3F1

node "analysis-host" #FFFCF5 {
  database "results/\nper-request records" as RES
  component "Record Joiner\n+ figure scripts" as AN
  component "Discrete-Event Simulator" as SIM
}

CFG -right-> REP
TR -right-> REP
CFG -down-> RM
REP -down-> CLI

CLI -down- LAN : <<gRPC>>  **Submit**\n<<gRPC>>  **full response, direct from worker (F-11)**
SCHED -down- LAN : <<gRPC>>  **Dispatch**  ·  **Heartbeat**

NA -[hidden]right-> NB
NB -[hidden]right-> NC
NC -[hidden]right-> ND

LAN -down- NA
LAN -down- NB
LAN -down- NC
LAN -down- ND

WA -down-> EA
WB -down-> EB
WC -down-> EC
WD -down-> ED

TR .right.> SIM : same trace replayed\nin simulation (F-17)
NA .down.> RES : <<offline>> JSONL
ND .down.> RES : <<offline>> JSONL
SCHED .down.> RES : <<offline>> JSONL\ndecision records (F-3)
CLI .down.> RES : <<offline>> JSONL
SIM -down-> RES
RES -right-> AN

note right of SCHED
  Single point of failure, accepted and justified: milliseconds
  of scheduling work against seconds of worker service time,
  at 3–5 nodes (F-12).
end note

note right of NA
  Engine and quantization are **constant across every node**. R is set by
  hardware class and by per-node offload and thread configuration (F-9a),
  which is what makes it tunable on physical hardware rather than only in
  simulation. Offload values are illustrative; final values from Week 2.
end note

note bottom of VGAP
  The engine gap is **measured once and reported as a magnitude**, not
  assumed away (F-9b). vLLM participates in no policy comparison and
  appears in no figure other than the engine-gap result. It bounds
  external validity (threat R9).
end note

note bottom of RES
  Host clocks are **not** synchronised. Every process reports only
  durations it measured itself; the stages are reassembled offline
  by joining on req_id (F-18).
end note

legend right
  <color:#BFD6D1>███</color>  system under study
  <color:#EBC98F>███</color>  instrumentation
  <color:#C9C9C2>███</color>  reused third-party runtime
endlegend
@enduml
